# Fingerprints gitleaks must not re-report, as <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>.
#
# Scope note: these only matter to the scheduled full-history scan. On push
# and pull_request gitleaks diffs the new commits, where neither line is
# touched, which is why those runs were already green while the nightly one
# was not.
#
# Entries are pinned to one commit, file, rule and line each. That is
# deliberate: editing either line changes its fingerprint and the finding
# comes back for review, rather than a path or rule allowlist silently
# covering whatever lands there later.

